{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\nimport Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.ChiralHodgeCartanBridge\n\nRepresentation dictionary for the Hodge phase, chirality axis, and Cartan\ninvolution.\n\nThis file deliberately separates:\n\n* Hodge/Hestenes phase candidates, which may satisfy `*² = -1` only after a\n  degree/signature convention is supplied;\n* chirality/grading involutions `Γ`, which satisfy `Γ² = 1`;\n* Cartan involutions `θΓ(X) = Γ X Γ`, which split operators into even and odd\n  sectors;\n* phase-induced Cartan involutions `θK(X) = -K X K` when the supplied Hodge\n  phase satisfies `K² = -1`.\n\nThe theorem-level payload is purely algebraic:\n\n```text\nD Γ = -Γ D  ->  D² Γ = Γ D².\n```\n\nThus a Dirac/supercharge candidate is Cartan-odd while its square is\nCartan-even, once the chirality involution is supplied.\n\nThe file also records the sign correction for square-minus-one Hodge phases:\n`K` itself is not a chirality involution, but `X ↦ -K X K` is an involution when\n`K² = -1`.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.ChiralHodgeCartanBridge\n\n/-- Carrier for the representation dictionary. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier (Op : Type*) where\n  /-- Hodge/Hestenes phase axis, usually square-minus-one. -/\n  hodgePhase : Op\n\n  /-- Chirality / spectral grading axis. -/\n  gamma : Op\n\n  /-- Dirac/supercharge candidate. -/\n  dirac : Op\n\n  /-- Laplacian / even Hamiltonian candidate. -/\n  laplacian : Op\n\n/--\nHodge/Hestenes phase convention.\n\nThis is external because `*² = -1` depends on dimension, degree, and signature.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsHodgePhase {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op) : Prop :=\n  C.hodgePhase * C.hodgePhase = -(1 : Op)\n\n/-- Chirality axis is an involution. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsChiralityInvolution {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op) : Prop :=\n  C.gamma * C.gamma = 1\n\n/-- Dirac/supercharge is odd for the chirality axis. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsDiracOddForChirality {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op) : Prop :=\n  C.dirac * C.gamma = -(C.gamma * C.dirac)\n\n/-- Laplacian/even Hamiltonian is the square of the Dirac/supercharge. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsLaplacianFromDirac {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op) : Prop :=\n  C.laplacian = C.dirac * C.dirac\n\n/-- Cartan involution generated by a chirality axis. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef thetaGamma {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (gamma X : Op) : Op :=\n  gamma * X * gamma\n\n/-- Backwards-compatible name for the chirality-generated Cartan involution. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef theta {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (gamma X : Op) : Op :=\n  thetaGamma gamma X\n\n/-- Cartan involution induced by a square-minus-one Hodge/Hestenes phase. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef thetaPhase {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (K X : Op) : Op :=\n  -(K * X * K)\n\n/-- Cartan-even sector: fixed by `θ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsCartanEven {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (gamma X : Op) : Prop :=\n  thetaGamma gamma X = X\n\n/-- Cartan-odd sector: negated by `θ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsCartanOdd {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (gamma X : Op) : Prop :=\n  thetaGamma gamma X = -X\n\n/-- Phase-Cartan-even sector: fixed by `θK(X) = -KXK`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsPhaseCartanEven {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (K X : Op) : Prop :=\n  thetaPhase K X = X\n\n/-- Phase-Cartan-odd sector: negated by `θK(X) = -KXK`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsPhaseCartanOdd {Op : Type*} [Ring Op] (K X : Op) : Prop :=\n  thetaPhase K X = -X\n\n/-- A chirality involution produces an involutive Cartan action. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem theta_involutive\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (gamma X : Op)\n    (hGamma : gamma * gamma = 1) :\n    thetaGamma gamma (thetaGamma gamma X) = X := by\n  unfold thetaGamma\n  calc\n    gamma * (gamma * X * gamma) * gamma =\n        (gamma * gamma) * X * (gamma * gamma) := by\n      noncomm_ring\n    _ = 1 * X * 1 := by\n      rw [hGamma]\n    _ = X := by\n      simp\n\n/-- Compatibility readback for the legacy `theta` spelling. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem theta_alias_eq_thetaGamma\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (gamma X : Op) :\n    theta gamma X = thetaGamma gamma X := by\n  rfl\n\n/-- A square-minus-one Hodge phase produces an involutive Cartan action. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem thetaPhase_involutive\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (K X : Op)\n    (hK : K * K = -(1 : Op)) :\n    thetaPhase K (thetaPhase K X) = X := by\n  unfold thetaPhase\n  calc\n    -(K * (-(K * X * K)) * K) =\n        (K * K) * X * (K * K) := by\n      noncomm_ring\n    _ = (-(1 : Op)) * X * (-(1 : Op)) := by\n      rw [hK]\n    _ = X := by\n      simp\n\n/-- Anticommutation with `Γ` is equivalent to Cartan-oddness under `θ(X)=ΓXΓ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem cartanOdd_of_anticommutes_gamma\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (gamma D : Op)\n    (hGamma : gamma * gamma = 1)\n    (hOdd : D * gamma = -(gamma * D)) :\n    IsCartanOdd gamma D := by\n  unfold IsCartanOdd thetaGamma\n  calc\n    gamma * D * gamma = gamma * (D * gamma) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = gamma * (-(gamma * D)) := by\n      rw [hOdd]\n    _ = -((gamma * gamma) * D) := by\n      simp [mul_assoc]\n    _ = -D := by\n      rw [hGamma]\n      simp\n\n/-- Algebraic core: a chiral-odd Dirac/supercharge has a chirality-even square. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem dirac_square_commutes_gamma\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (D gamma : Op)\n    (hOdd : D * gamma = -(gamma * D)) :\n    (D * D) * gamma = gamma * (D * D) := by\n  calc\n    (D * D) * gamma = D * (D * gamma) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = D * (-(gamma * D)) := by\n      rw [hOdd]\n    _ = -(D * (gamma * D)) := by\n      simp\n    _ = -((D * gamma) * D) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = -((-(gamma * D)) * D) := by\n      rw [hOdd]\n    _ = gamma * (D * D) := by\n      simp [mul_assoc]\n\n/-- Commutation with `Γ` implies Cartan-evenness under `θΓ(X)=ΓXΓ`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem cartanEven_of_commutes_gamma\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (gamma X : Op)\n    (hGamma : gamma * gamma = 1)\n    (hComm : X * gamma = gamma * X) :\n    IsCartanEven gamma X := by\n  unfold IsCartanEven thetaGamma\n  calc\n    gamma * X * gamma = gamma * (X * gamma) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = gamma * (gamma * X) := by\n      rw [hComm]\n    _ = (gamma * gamma) * X := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = X := by\n      rw [hGamma]\n      simp\n\n/-- Anticommutation with a square-minus-one phase is phase-Cartan-odd. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem phaseCartanOdd_of_anticommutes\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (K X : Op)\n    (hK : K * K = -(1 : Op))\n    (hAnti : X * K = -(K * X)) :\n    IsPhaseCartanOdd K X := by\n  unfold IsPhaseCartanOdd thetaPhase\n  calc\n    -(K * X * K) = -(K * (X * K)) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = -(K * (-(K * X))) := by\n      rw [hAnti]\n    _ = (K * K) * X := by\n      simp [mul_assoc]\n    _ = (-(1 : Op)) * X := by\n      rw [hK]\n    _ = -X := by\n      simp\n\n/-- Commutation with a square-minus-one phase is phase-Cartan-even. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem phaseCartanEven_of_commutes\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (K X : Op)\n    (hK : K * K = -(1 : Op))\n    (hComm : X * K = K * X) :\n    IsPhaseCartanEven K X := by\n  unfold IsPhaseCartanEven thetaPhase\n  calc\n    -(K * X * K) = -(K * (X * K)) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = -(K * (K * X)) := by\n      rw [hComm]\n    _ = -((K * K) * X) := by\n      rw [mul_assoc]\n    _ = -((-(1 : Op)) * X) := by\n      rw [hK]\n    _ = X := by\n      simp\n\n/-- If `D` is chiral-odd, then `D²` is Cartan-even. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem dirac_square_cartanEven_of_dirac_odd\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (D gamma : Op)\n    (hGamma : gamma * gamma = 1)\n    (hOdd : D * gamma = -(gamma * D)) :\n    IsCartanEven gamma (D * D) :=\n  cartanEven_of_commutes_gamma gamma (D * D) hGamma\n    (dirac_square_commutes_gamma D gamma hOdd)\n\n/-- Carrier-level readback: `dirac` is Cartan-odd. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem carrier_dirac_cartanOdd\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op)\n    (hGamma : IsChiralityInvolution C)\n    (hOdd : IsDiracOddForChirality C) :\n    IsCartanOdd C.gamma C.dirac :=\n  cartanOdd_of_anticommutes_gamma C.gamma C.dirac hGamma hOdd\n\n/-- Carrier-level readback: the Dirac square is Cartan-even. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem carrier_dirac_square_cartanEven\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op)\n    (hGamma : IsChiralityInvolution C)\n    (hOdd : IsDiracOddForChirality C) :\n    IsCartanEven C.gamma (C.dirac * C.dirac) :=\n  dirac_square_cartanEven_of_dirac_odd C.dirac C.gamma hGamma hOdd\n\n/-- Carrier-level readback: if `Δ = D²`, then `Δ` is Cartan-even. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem laplacian_even_of_dirac_odd\n    {Op : Type*} [Ring Op]\n    (C : ChiralHodgeCartanCarrier Op)\n    (hGamma : IsChiralityInvolution C)\n    (hOdd : IsDiracOddForChirality C)\n    (hLap : IsLaplacianFromDirac C) :\n    IsCartanEven C.gamma C.laplacian := by\n  rw [hLap]\n  exact carrier_dirac_square_cartanEven C hGamma hOdd\n\n/-- Carrier for left/right anomaly charge readout. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nstructure ChiralAnomalyChargeCarrier (Op : Type*) where\n  /-- Right/range anomaly current. -/\n  chiR : Op\n\n  /-- Left/domain anomaly current. -/\n  chiL : Op\n\n  /-- Net chiral supercharge. -/\n  Q : Op\n\n/-- Net chiral charge law `Q = χ_R - χ_L`. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ndef IsNetChiralCharge {Op : Type*} [Sub Op]\n    (C : ChiralAnomalyChargeCarrier Op) : Prop :=\n  C.Q = C.chiR - C.chiL\n\n/-- Direct readback of the supplied net chiral charge law. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem netChiralCharge_eq_chiR_sub_chiL\n    {Op : Type*} [Sub Op]\n    (C : ChiralAnomalyChargeCarrier Op)\n    (hQ : IsNetChiralCharge C) :\n    C.Q = C.chiR - C.chiL :=\n  hQ\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.ChiralHodgeCartanBridge\n","mtime":1778706415750}